  "id": "positive-hallucination",
  "term": "positive hallucination",
  "definition": "In this historical source, a positive hallucination is the ordinary kind of hallucination: perceiving an object, voice, or scene as present when it is not actually there. It is contrasted with negative hallucination, in which something real is not perceived.",
